# PostPylot — Cost Principles

Target: **$0–15/month** for the MVP. Optimize for effective results at near-zero cost by
using open-source, self-hosted, and free-tier technology wherever feasible. See
[`docs/CONSTITUTION.md`](../../docs/CONSTITUTION.md) and [`docs/adr/`](../../docs/adr/).

## Default to free / open-source

- **Jobs:** pg-boss on the existing Supabase Postgres. No paid queue. No cron in the app
  runtime. (ADR 001)
- **TTS:** Piper (MVP) → Kokoro (quality) self-hosted. ElevenLabs is opt-in premium only.
  (ADR 002)
- **Captions:** local Whisper (e.g. whisper.cpp) in the worker. No paid transcription.
- **Images:** Satori + Resvg + Sharp template graphics. No paid image APIs in MVP.
- **Video:** Remotion + FFmpeg in the worker. No paid render services.
- **LLM:** Gemini free/cheap tier first, OpenAI fallback. Batch and cache to cut tokens.
- **Hosting:** Vercel free tier (web) + one small always-on worker host.
- **Data/Storage/Auth:** Supabase free tier (Postgres, Storage, Auth, RLS).

## Rules

- Prefer self-host over managed paid services until quality or scale genuinely forces an
  upgrade — and record that upgrade in an ADR.
- Never add a paid dependency by default. If a paid path exists, make it opt-in and keep a
  free default working.
- Cache and reuse AI output, media, and analytics pulls. Avoid re-generating identical
  content; dedupe topics.
- Respect provider free-tier limits (rate limits, batch sizes) in agent and job design.
- When proposing a new dependency, state its cost and the free alternative you rejected.
